{
  "_comment": [
    "The single shared type definition for the browser/API boundary.",
    "",
    "The Go handlers emit this JSON and the dashboard reads it, and nothing in",
    "either language would notice a renamed field: it would surface as",
    "`undefined` in a browser rather than as a build failure. So this file is",
    "the contract, and both sides are pinned to it - pkg/dashboard/contract_test.go",
    "fails the build if a Go struct's JSON tags drift from what is written here,",
    "and api.js warns in the console if a response carries fields this file does",
    "not describe.",
    "",
    "Changing a field means changing it here, in the Go struct, and in the",
    "screen that reads it. That is the point: the change is not silent."
  ],
  "types": {
    "Agent": [
      "id",
      "name",
      "description",
      "model",
      "base_url",
      "system_prompt",
      "user_prompt",
      "tools",
      "max_steps",
      "max_tokens",
      "max_duration_seconds",
      "secret_name",
      "context_mode",
      "context_runs",
      "enabled",
      "created_at",
      "updated_at"
    ],
    "AgentOverview": [
      "id",
      "name",
      "description",
      "model",
      "base_url",
      "system_prompt",
      "user_prompt",
      "tools",
      "max_steps",
      "max_tokens",
      "max_duration_seconds",
      "secret_name",
      "context_mode",
      "context_runs",
      "enabled",
